<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Ahmanson '98 estimate raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Ahmanson '98 estimate raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>- Sanford Bernstein analyst Jonathan Gray raised his 1998 forecast for H.F. Ahmanson to $3.40 a share from $3.30 a sahre to reflect lower credit costs.</p>
<p>- Gray said Ahmanson's first quarter results exceeded his estimates of operating earnings per share.Gray had forecast $0.75 in operating EPS excluding an expected $0.08 per share gain on sale of some savings branches in Arizona. The $0.79 in operating EPS reflected a sharp drop in credit losses.</p>
</text>
